  "summary": "A British social research project that began in 1937. It relied mainly on volunteer correspondents and some paid investigators. Photography was a small part of it. Humphrey Spender photographed Bolton for it, and this is the only link to documentary photography here. The original group ran to the mid-1960s. A firm took the name in 1949. The University of Sussex relaunched the project in 1981.",
